; Test: Conditional swap (bubble sort step)
; ==========================================
;
; Demonstrates: Swapping two facts conditionally
; Based on test from kernel/src/main.rs:1537 (odd_even_sort)

; Setup: Order relation and two items
(lt B A)  ; B < A (meaning A should come after B)

; Test: Swap if out of order
(exec 0
  (, (item 0 $x)
     (item 1 $y)
     (lt $y $x))   ; If y < x, they're out of order
  (O (- (item 0 $x))
     (- (item 1 $y))
     (+ (item 0 $y))
     (+ (item 1 $x))))

(item 0 A)
(item 1 B)

; Expected output:
; (item 0 B)
; (item 1 A)
;
; The items are swapped because B < A in the order relation.
; This is one step of bubble sort!
